1
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,552
A big fund buys ten million worth of stock today.

2
00:00:09,003 --> 00:00:12,007
In the evening, the boss asks one question.

3
00:00:12,457 --> 00:00:16,009
Did you buy cheaper or more expensive than the average price?

4
00:00:16,459 --> 00:00:22,650
The line that measures that average price is called VWAP.

5
00:00:23,650 --> 00:00:28,405
Hello, this is episode eight of the SPIDER Order Flow series.

6
00:00:28,854 --> 00:00:33,766
Last time we saw Volume Profile: how much traded at each price.

7
00:00:34,216 --> 00:00:39,362
Today we build a line from that volume, one that moves with price all day.

8
00:00:40,362 --> 00:00:42,791
Say three trades happened today.

9
00:00:43,241 --> 00:00:50,164
10 lots at 100, 10 at 102, and 180 at 104.

10
00:00:50,614 --> 00:00:53,853
A simple average gives 102.

11
00:00:54,303 --> 00:01:00,337
But most of the volume traded at 104. So the real average cannot be 102.

12
00:01:01,337 --> 00:01:04,890
So each price is weighted by its volume.

13
00:01:05,340 --> 00:01:10,172
Price times volume, summed, divided by total volume.

14
00:01:10,622 --> 00:01:15,062
Here the answer is about 103.7.

15
00:01:15,512 --> 00:01:22,670
That is VWAP. Volume Weighted Average Price.

16
00:01:23,670 --> 00:01:29,862
On the chart, VWAP is a line that starts counting from the start of the day.

17
00:01:30,312 --> 00:01:37,077
With each new candle, new price and volume are added, and the line moves a little.

18
00:01:37,527 --> 00:01:43,092
In the morning it moves fast. As the day goes on, it slows down.

19
00:01:43,541 --> 00:01:49,184
Because the more volume already counted, the less one new trade can move it.

20
00:01:50,184 --> 00:01:54,232
Why do big players watch VWAP so closely?

21
00:01:54,683 --> 00:01:58,889
Because their work is often measured against VWAP.

22
00:01:59,339 --> 00:02:06,261
A buyer wants to buy below VWAP. A seller wants to sell above it.

23
00:02:06,711 --> 00:02:11,466
That is why large orders often trade around VWAP.

24
00:02:12,466 --> 00:02:14,503
Now the simplest reading.

25
00:02:14,953 --> 00:02:23,077
Price above VWAP: buyers are paying more than average today. Buyers in control.

26
00:02:23,527 --> 00:02:28,046
Price below VWAP: sellers in control.

27
00:02:28,495 --> 00:02:36,046
And if price keeps crossing VWAP, nobody is in control. The market is undecided.

28
00:02:37,046 --> 00:02:42,375
VWAP often comes with bands above and below.

29
00:02:42,825 --> 00:02:51,184
They show how far price has stretched from VWAP. These are standard deviation bands.

30
00:02:51,634 --> 00:02:57,041
The first band is normal distance. The second band is a big stretch.

31
00:02:57,491 --> 00:03:04,022
Price at the second band often snaps back a bit like a rubber band. But not always.

32
00:03:04,472 --> 00:03:09,304
On a trend day, price can hug the band all day.

33
00:03:10,304 --> 00:03:15,059
Another form: Anchored VWAP.

34
00:03:15,509 --> 00:03:20,498
Here the count starts not from the day open but from a chosen candle.

35
00:03:20,948 --> 00:03:25,546
Like a big news candle, or a major low.

36
00:03:25,995 --> 00:03:33,885
It shows the average price of everyone who came in after that moment, and whether they are in profit or loss.

37
00:03:34,885 --> 00:03:42,042
Important: forex and spot gold have no real volume, as we saw in Episode 6.

38
00:03:42,492 --> 00:03:49,807
So VWAP there is built from tick volume. It is an estimate, not an exact count.

39
00:03:50,257 --> 00:03:54,541
For a real VWAP, look at the futures chart.

40
00:03:55,541 --> 00:03:58,858
Three common mistakes with VWAP.

41
00:03:59,308 --> 00:04:06,152
One: treating VWAP alone as a signal. It is a map, not a trigger.

42
00:04:06,602 --> 00:04:14,152
Two: trusting VWAP in the first minutes of the day. It is still raw then.

43
00:04:14,602 --> 00:04:19,852
Three: fading the band again and again on a trend day.

44
00:04:20,852 --> 00:04:22,420
So, today's summary.

45
00:04:22,870 --> 00:04:31,699
VWAP is the volume-weighted average price: price times volume over total volume.

46
00:04:32,149 --> 00:04:39,071
Above means buyers in control, below means sellers. Bands show the stretch.

47
00:04:39,521 --> 00:04:46,444
Anchored VWAP counts from a chosen moment. In forex and gold, it is only an estimate.

48
00:04:47,444 --> 00:04:55,411
Next episode: session profiles. Asia, London and New York, each with its own character.

49
00:04:55,861 --> 00:05:00,694
